SOUND-SEQUENCER ARM-GATE PRODUCER (FUN_1000_1042, asm 0x11042) reconstructed.

The menu-music sequencer is gated by a producer/consumer SEMAPHORE at the arm word DGROUP:0x23e:
the SOUNDDVR timer-ISR (driver 0x3dd, patch 356) runs its 7-voice scan only while `cmpw ss:0x23e,2`
holds, and `decw ss:0x23e` (0x40d) drops it 2->1 each pass.  FUN_1000_1042 is the PRODUCER that bumps
it back toward 2 (`incb [ss:0x23e]`, SS=DGROUP=0x1c00).

Ghidra base-lost the byte target to `DAT_2000_bcce` (the bogus SS=0x2ba9 segment context, the
patch-356 class): 0x2bcce instead of the real DGROUP:0x23e = linear 0x1c23e.  The function IS live in
the engine fmap ({0x11042u,&FUN_1000_1042}) and is dispatched indirectly by a sound-service vector, but
the port never reaches that dispatch, so the shim drives it per sound-tick (fist_sb.c fist_snd_isr_tick)
-- the faithful hardware-timer equivalent (we own the PIT/INT-8 layer).

asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin:
  11042: push ds
  11043: push ss ; pop ds          ; ds = ss = DGROUP
  11045: incb [0x23e]              ; ++byte[DGROUP:0x23e]
  11049: je 0x11056                ; overflow (was 0xff -> 0): stc; pop ds; ret
  ... (the 0x1104b nop/jmp/mov bx,bx/jb dead tail never loops -- incb sets no CF)
  11054: pop ds ; ret             ; CF=0 success
Net: `if (++byte[0x23e] == 0) CF=1 else CF=0`.  The caller (the sound-service dispatcher) discards CF;
we publish it to g_fist_cf for faithfulness.

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -39307,14 +39307,13 @@
 void __allregs FUN_1000_1042(void)
 
 {
-  bool in_CF;
-  
-  do {
-    DAT_2000_bcce = DAT_2000_bcce + '\x01';
-    if (DAT_2000_bcce == '\0') {
-      return;
-    }
-  } while (in_CF);
+  /* PATCH 357: the sound-sequencer ARM-GATE PRODUCER (asm 0x11042: push ss;pop ds; incb [ss:0x23e]).
+     SS=DS=DGROUP(0x1c00); Ghidra base-lost the byte target to DAT_2000_bcce (bogus SS=0x2ba9 context).
+     Real target = the arm word's low byte at DGROUP:0x23e = linear 0x1c23e.  CF=1 on byte overflow. */
+  extern unsigned char g_mem[]; extern unsigned char g_fist_cf;
+  unsigned char v = (unsigned char)(g_mem[0x1c23e] + 1);
+  g_mem[0x1c23e] = v;
+  g_fist_cf = (unsigned char)(v == 0);
   return;
 }
 
